[037] indent=0 block=36ddbe27 H2
      "Forecasting domain underperformance is not representative of MC Beta " {b}
[038] indent=0 block=36ddbe27 H2
      "performance" {b}
[039] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "1. "
      "Forecasting questions rely on information contained in the context " {b}
[040] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "   "
      "layer" {b}
      " (cross-validation runs, forecast model methodology documents), "
[041] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "   "
      "which is not deployed in the MT environment, and has not been "
[042] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "   "
      "invested in."
[043] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "▾ "
      "Example" {b}
[044] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " \"For ERCOT__DART__PROF__UNIVARIATE__DAYZER config version "
[045] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "1.2, explain at a high level what PROF does and which inputs it uses.”"
[046] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "Context needed:" {b}
      " documents like "
      "PROF: Probabilistic Regime Overlayed " {href=https://app.notion.com/p/196dbe27599280fe821aef46de0dd9fb}
[047] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "Forecasting " {href=https://app.notion.com/p/196dbe27599280fe821aef46de0dd9fb}
      " "
[048] indent=0 block=36cdbe27
      "[image]" {i fg=#9b9a97}
[049] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "1. "
      "Flawed experiment design" {b}
      " - questions in the dataset asked about "
[050] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "   "
      "models and information that MC Beta users would not be privy to"
[051] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "1. "
      "These questions were closer to how we would expect an internal "
[052] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "   "
      "scientist to use the chat. In that context, it did not perform "
[053] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "   "
      "well. "
[054] indent=0 block=36ddbe27
      "▾ "
      "Examples" {b}
[055] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "\"For ERCOT__DART__PROF__SMOOTH_UNIVARIATE__DAYZER config version 1.0, "
[056] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "list the Dayzer fundamentals and other input models used for operating"
[057] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "day 2026-05-15.”"
[058] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "\"For ERCOT__RTMEC__PROF__UNIVARIATE__DAYZER config version 3.1, "
[059] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "summarize analyses completed between 2026-05-01 and 2026-05-15 and "
[060] indent=2 block=36ddbe27
      "identify the most promising version by validation MAE.”"
