[135] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "nodes using PROF-Dayzer with Featurestore features."
[136] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[137] indent=6 block=36cdbe27 H3
      "What I can't provide" {b}
[138] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "The three-way hourly comparison you're asking for — "
      "EQ DAYZER vs. " {b}
[139] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "ERCOT published forecast vs. external vendor" {b}
      " — isn't available in "
[140] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the agentic context for 2026-05-15. Specifically:"
[141] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "Hourly forecast values" {b}
      " from the DAYZER run are not surfaced in "
[142] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "the context layer (the run metadata confirms it completed, but "
[143] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "the output price curves aren't stored here)."
[144] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "ERCOT's published DA LMP forecast" {b}
      " (e.g., from the ERCOT DAM or "
[145] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "their public forecast products) doesn't have a corresponding "
[146] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "EQRN in the context."
[147] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "External vendor forecasts" {b}
      " — no vendor forecast EQRNs (e.g., Wood"
[148] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "Mackenzie, Ascend, or similar) are registered in the context for"
[149] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "this date."
[150] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "To do this comparison, you'd need to pull the DAYZER output "
[151] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "directly from S3 (the deployment writes to the standard forecast "
[152] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "bucket), layer in ERCOT's published DA clearing prices or their "
[153] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "pre-market forecast, and add the vendor feed. If you can point me "
[154] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "to where the vendor data lives or share the hub you want to focus "
[155] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "on (HB_NORTH, HB_WEST, HB_SOUTH, HB_HOUSTON), I can help structure"
[156] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the analysis once the data is accessible."
