[162] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "What went well" {b}
[163] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▪ "
      "The agent has the domain knowledge to deliver causal chain answers"
[164] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "• "
      "\"Wind + solar oversupply → exceeds local load → transmission " {i}
[165] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "  "
      "constraints prevent export → DA prices go negative to suppress " {i}
[166] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "  "
      "generation.”" {i}
[167] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "What needs fixing" {b}
[168] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▪ "
      "Lean more into analysis, rather than description"
[169] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "• "
      "\"The answer describes what happened, not what was at risk\"" {i}
      " "
[170] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "Examples" {b}
[171] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Good"
[172] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " "
[173] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "\"For ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15, why are LMPs forecast so low " {i}
[174] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "in DA at HB_WEST?\"" {i}
[175] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Response: " {b}
[176] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "“The short answer: a classic West Texas renewable oversupply " {i}
[177] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "event. Strong southerly winds combined with robust solar " {i}
[178] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "irradiance during daylight hours pushed generation well above " {i}
[179] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "local load, creating significant negative-price hours in the DA " {i}
[180] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "market.\n[Followed by a DA vs. RT price table covering HE9–HE18 " {i}
[181] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "across HB_WEST, HB_NORTH, and HB_HOUSTON, then three drivers: " {i}
[182] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "wind, solar, transmission congestion]" {i}
[183] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nHB_WEST was negative or near-zero for 10 consecutive hours " {i}
[184] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "(HE9–HE18 CDT), while HB_NORTH and HB_HOUSTON were clearing " {i}
[185] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "$14–$38/MWh during the same window. That's a massive basis spread " {i}
[186] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "driven by local congestion.”" {i}
[187] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Bad"
[188] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
      " "
[189] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "\"For ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15, which Load Zone is forecasted" {i}
[190] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "to have the highest peak load, and which hours?\"" {i}
[191] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Response:" {b}
[192] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "“The load profiles are charted above. NORTH_ERCOT's dominance is " {i}
[193] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "clear throughout the day, with the gap widening significantly from" {i}
[194] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "HE14 onward into the evening peak. Let me know if you want to " {i}
[195] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "cross-reference with RT actuals or DA prices for that zone.”" {i}
[196] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Reviewer Comment:" {b}
[197] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "“No chart outputted. The answer never states which zone has the " {i}
[198] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "highest peak load or which hours. \"NORTH_ERCOT's dominance is " {i}
[199] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "clear throughout the day\" implies it's the answer, but the " {i}
[200] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "question asked for a specific zone and specific hours. neither is " {i}
[201] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "stated explicitly. A reader who needs this for a DA bid can't act " {i}
[202] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "on \"dominance is clear.””" {i}
