      "What went well" {b}
[209] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▪ "
      "Performed well in broad summarization questions, and well-scoped "
[210] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "  "
      "objective questions"
[211] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "What needs fixing" {b}
[212] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▪ "
      "Wrong DART sign convention - giving RT - DA"
[213] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▪ "
      "Wrong metrics comparisons - comparing DA forecasts with RT actuals"
[214] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▪ "
      "Data access - when asked about the existing like-days, the agent "
[215] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "  "
      "claimed it couldn’t compute"
[216] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "Examples" {b}
[217] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Good"
[218] indent=6 block=36bdbe27
      "Question:" {b}
[219] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\"How did ERCOT real-time prices settle relative to DA forecasts by" {i}
[220] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "hub on 2026-05-15?”" {i}
[221] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Response:" {b}
[222] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Here's the DA vs. RT settlement picture for May 15." {i}
[223] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Key themes:" {b i}
[224] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "West/Panhandle — RT ran well above DA overnight, then flipped" {b i}
[225] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nHB_WEST and HB_PAN were the most notable deviations. RT beat DA by" {i}
[226] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "$17–19/MWh in the overnight hours (HE1–HE8), likely reflecting " {i}
[227] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "lower-than-forecast wind output when DA priced in strong " {i}
[228] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "generation. Both hubs then flipped negative in the evening " {i}
[229] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "(HE19–HE20) before spiking again at HE22–HE24." {i}
[230] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "South — persistent RT discount through the afternoon" {b i}
      "\nHB_SOUTH was " {i}
[231] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the weakest performer relative to DA. RT ran $10–15/MWh below DA " {i}
[232] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "from HE10 through HE16 — solar likely overperformed DA " {i}
[233] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "expectations, suppressing real-time prices. The daily average gap " {i}
[234] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "was -$5.48/MWh, the largest negative DART of any hub." {i}
[235] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Houston — RT outperformed DA in the afternoon peak" {b i}
      "\nHB_HOUSTON was " {i}
[236] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the only load-zone hub to finish the day with a positive DART " {i}
[237] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "(+$0.93/MWh). The afternoon ramp (HE15–HE18) saw RT exceed DA by " {i}
[238] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "up to $14.52/MWh, pointing to tighter supply conditions in the " {i}
[239] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Houston pocket than the DA anticipated." {i}
[240] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "North — roughly flat on the day" {b i}
      "\nHB_NORTH tracked DA closely, with a" {i}
[241] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "modest -$0.87/MWh daily average. The afternoon hours showed mild " {i}
[242] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "RT premiums, but midday solar suppression offset those gains." {i}
[243] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[244] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Want me to break any of these hubs down to the node level, or pull" {i}
[245] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "the DART spread series directly for a specific path?" {i}
[246] indent=4 block=36bdbe27
      "▾ "
      "Bad"
