      "└───────┴─────────────┴───────┴──────────────────────────────────┘" {fg=#9b9a97}
[266] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "What this tells you about DA bid behavior:" {b i}
[267] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "The " {i}
      "midday DA premium (HE9–HE13)" {b i}
      " — up to $8.21 at HE12 — is " {i}
[268] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "consistent with bidders pricing in solar uncertainty. DA cleared" {i}
[269] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "well above where RT settled, suggesting the market priced a risk" {i}
[270] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "premium for afternoon solar variability that didn't materialize " {i}
[271] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "as severely in RT." {i}
[272] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "The " {i}
      "HE15–HE17 reversal" {b i}
      " (RT > DA by up to $8.70) points to an " {i}
[273] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "underestimation of the evening ramp in DA — the opposite effect," {i}
[274] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "where RT tightened faster than DA anticipated." {i}
[275] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "• "
      "DAM volumes" {b i}
      " show buy-side demand peaking in HE17–HE22 " {i}
[276] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "(~17,500–18,300 MWh) with sell-side heaviest in HE9–HE13 " {i}
[277] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "(~5,000–5,300 MWh), consistent with participants locking in DA " {i}
[278] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "  "
      "sales during the solar window." {i}
[279] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────" {fg=#9b9a97}
[280] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "If you're working with a specific model or framework that uses " {i}
[281] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\"uncertainty penalization\" as a defined term — e.g., a stochastic " {i}
[282] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "bidding model or a specific EQ methodology — let me know and I can" {i}
[283] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "pull the relevant context. I can also break this down by " {i}
[284] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "node-level prices within the North zone if the hub view isn't " {i}
[285] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "granular enough." {i}
[286] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "Reviewer Comment:" {b}
[287] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "This response erodes my confidence in the chatbot. Question 2 was " {i}
[288] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "nearly the same; but generated this response:\nNo strategy run data " {i}
[289] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "found for ERCOT operating day 2026-05-15 at HB_NORTH." {i}
[290] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "I see how this response (likely) doesn't rely on bid data at all, " {i}
[291] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "and just uses DART trends to speak at a high level about expected " {i}
[292] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "bidding behavior. But that doesn't answer the question of \"how " {i}
[293] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "did\", it answers the question \"how could\"." {i}
[294] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nAdditionally, it's unclear if the data referenced in the response " {i}
[295] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "is forecast or actuals." {i}
[296] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nIf actuals: this response is not helpful, as it doesn't include " {i}
[297] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "any aspect of uncertainty." {i}
[298] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "\nIf forecasts: a point forecast is always an estimate, but it " {i}
[299] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "doesn't capture uncertainty. What is the agent using to identify " {i}
[300] indent=6 block=36cdbe27
      "uncertainty?" {i}
